        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "6fa143c1-eb51-57d1-84f7-9fe1968c5fbb",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Albany, Albany County, New York, Madison, Wisconsin, Colonie\n- Airports and Bases: Albany International Airport, Dane County Regional Airport, Truax Field Air National Guard Base\n- Transportation Systems: Interstate 687, I-90, I-87\n\nFacts:\n- Albany International Airport is a public airport located seven miles northwest of Albany in Albany County, New York, United States.\n- Dane County Regional Airport, also called Truax Field, is a civil-military airport located six miles northeast of downtown Madison, Wisconsin.\n- Truax Field Air National Guard Base is a military facility located at Dane County Regional Airport.\n- Interstate 687 was a proposed highway that would have connected I-90 in Albany to I-87 near Albany International Airport in Colonie.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "66505d7c-0d79-59ea-9d31-b780ce467702",
        "text": "Page: Albany International Airport. Sentence: Albany International Airport (IATA: ALB, ICAO: KALB, FAA LID: ALB) is a public airport seven miles (11 km) northwest of Albany, in Albany County, New York, United States.\nPage: Dane County Regional Airport. Sentence: Dane County Regional Airport (DCRA) (IATA: MSN, ICAO: KMSN, FAA LID: MSN) (Truax Field) is a civil-military airport located six miles northeast of downtown Madison, the capital of Wisconsin.\nPage: Interstate 687. Sentence: The highway would have connected I-90 in Albany to I-87 near Albany International Airport in Colonie.\nPage: Truax Field Air National Guard Base. Sentence: Truax Field Air National Guard Base (IATA: MSN, ICAO: KMSN, FAA LID: MSN) , also known as Truax Field, is a military facility located at Dane County Regional Airport.",
